ood Image Recognition in Apps for Nutrition Care#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)":[35,37],"#Evaluating the Quality and Comparative Validity of Manual Food Logging and Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Food Image Recognition in Apps for Nutrition Care#🔴 Bulgular (Kırmızı)#{1}":[36,37],"#Evaluating the Quality and Comparative Validity of Manual Food Logging and Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Food Image Recognition in Apps for Nutrition Care#🔵 Sonuç / Conclusions (Mavi)":[38,40],"#Evaluating the Quality and Comparative Validity of Manual Food Logging and Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Food Image Recognition in Apps for Nutrition Care#🟠 Limitasyonlar (Turuncu)":[41,42]},"outlinks":[{"title":"Görüntüle","target":"zotero://select/library/items/8B5II4RM","line":22},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/34WJJ22W?page=1&annotation=SYH4MSIB","line":33},{"title":"Sayfa 1","target":"zotero://open-pdf/library/items/34WJJ22W?page=1&annotation=N46EV4J7","line":36}],"metadata":{"Title":"Evaluating the Quality and Comparative Validity of Manual Food Logging and Artificial Intelligence-Enabled Food Image Recognition in Apps for Nutrition Care","Authors":"Xinyi Li, Annabelle Yin, Ha Young Choi, Virginia Chan, Margaret Allman-Farinelli, Juliana Chen","Year":2024,"DOI":"10.3390/nu16152573","Nitelik":null,"Alan":null,"Konu":null,"AI_Methodology":null,"Layer_Focus":null,"Model_Asamasi":null,"Proposed_Tool":null,"Methods":"AI. The top 200 free and paid nutrition-related apps from Australia’s Apple App and Google Play stores were screened (n = 800). Apps were assessed using MARS (quality) and ABACUS (behaviour change potential). Nutritional outputs from manual food logging and AI-enabled food-image recognition apps were compared with food records for Western, Asian, and Recommended diets.","Findings":"Apps with more AI integration demonstrated better functionality, but automatic energy estimations from AI-enabled food image recognition were inaccurate.","Conclusions":"","Limitations":"","User_Notes":""},"task_lines":[],"tasks":{},"codeblock_ranges":[],"last_embed":{"hash":"1auowuz","at":1774939664115}},"smart_blocks:liEvaluatingQualityComparative2024b.md#---frontmatter---": {"path":null,"embeddings":{"TaylorAI/bge-micro-v2":{"vec":[-0.03103769,-0.0138947,-0.01678058,-0.03583323,-0.00192826,0.03117827,-0.00401048,0.00952328,-0.04813866,-0.00799346,-0.01835646,-0.09488324,0.00861768,0.04748676,0.03820384,-0.02875123,0.0586751,0.0082,-0.01712102,-0.01305802,0.06562239,-0.0237566,0.00093785,-0.02474079,0.04912024,0.04322446,-0.03269306,-0.03706823,-0.06150085,-0.22867788,0.00201868,-0.0534078,0.06772146,-0.0258176,-0.01335676,0.01567996,-0.02872055,0.01451438,-0.08373886,0.00886536,0.06027727,-0.00779997,0.04402236,-0.01955318,-0.03445553,-0.02930333,-0.03427134,0.00019221,-0.0898082,0.01441953,0.01639277,-0.0188584,0.01324158,0.03248631,0.03572128,0.06032529,0.03238686,0.07395533,0.09597319,0.09018846,0.03530869,0.0633452,-0.19199312,0.06938156,0.0780646,0.00983291,-0.08371703,-0.05680767,-0.0419911,-0.04720329,-0.01180225,-0.00058198,0.0561579,-0.0009913,0.00632598,0.00812476,0.08120947,-0.03771345,-0.05334623,-0.06248178,-0.01217825,0.06156113,-0.02179055,0.0198301,-0.01713758,0.01520187,-0.03468109,-0.0053427,0.06562606,-0.05726879,0.02463475,-0.00212779,0.01071089,0.01924487,-0.0033181,-0.01550366,-0.02575535,0.01497898,-0.04957169,0.11466102,-0.00549062,-0.02517214,-0.03578021,-0.05271034,0.05319551,-0.0627767,0.00117993,-0.01945384,-0.05324917,0.06283827,-0.00122568,0.02398591,0.02170413,0.03496439,-0.00361073,0.04894482,0.0899433,0.00999699,0.05582263,-0.03426692,-0.04612563,0.01610175,0.04588609,-0.04155831,-0.01865819,0.01882971,-0.0036596,0.04682014,-0.02420192,-0.02104595,0.07238635,-0.0505242,-0.04924138,-0.02197567,0.0149995,0.01118534,0.00622745,0.02966703,0.00644075,0.07107464,-0.04950542,-0.01249386,0.02826028,-0.06238383,-0.04692731,0.13870466,0.02858867,0.04628739,-0.05800556,-0.05150934,0.05419126,0.01911402,-0.03956959,0.0